    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Tempo changes, and the two things called tempo (docs/prompts/72)." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// A tempo marking is notation: it is printed, it stands at a place, and some" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// markings are only words. The tempo *map* is a function from beats to" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// seconds that the performance integrates. They are derived from the same" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// declaration and they are not the same thing — which is why the third" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// marking below prints and moves no clock at all." },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// Three markings, of which two carry a metronome:" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//   1/4 = 60                 at the top" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//   1/4 = 120 \"Doppio movimento\"   at bar 3 — the music runs twice as fast" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//   \"Meno mosso\"             at bar 5 — a word, and nothing for the engine" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "//" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// So `--to lilypond` writes three `\\tempo` commands, `--to musicxml` writes" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// two `<sound tempo>` elements, and the MIDI file carries two set-tempo" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// events. The page says more than the clock does, which is the ordinary case" },
    { "kind": "comment", "text": "// and the one a fused design cannot represent." },
    { "kind": "piece", "text": "piece" },
    { "kind": "string", "text": "\"Tempo Changes\"" },
